  "chapter": 1,
  "sortOrder": 56001,
  "verseCount": 16,
  "aliases": [
    "Titus",
    "Tit"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "In hope of eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised before the world began;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "But hath in due times manifested his word through preaching, which is committed unto me according to the commandment of God our Saviour;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "To Titus, mine own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ our Saviour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as I had appointed thee:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "If any be blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children not accused of riot or unruly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of God; not selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught, that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For there are many unruly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre’s sake.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "One of themselves, even a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "This witness is true. Wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men, that turn from the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Unto the pure all things are pure: but unto them that are defiled and unbelieving is nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:titus:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "They profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Titus 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:1:16"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
